{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "Using 2021 CKD-EPI Creatinine equation (race-free).\n\nFemale, Cr = 1.1 mg/dL, age = 33.\n\nFor females: κ = 0.7, α = -0.241\nCr/κ = 1.1/0.7 = 1.5714\n\nSince Cr/κ > 1, use max term = (Cr/κ)^(-1.200)\n\neGFR = 142 × min(Cr/κ,1)^α × max(Cr/κ,1)^(-1.200) × 0.9938^age × 1.012\n\nmin(Cr/κ,1) = 1, so min term^α = 1\n\nmax term = 1.5714^(-1.200)\nln(1.5714) = 0.4520\n× -1.2 = -0.5424\nexp(-0.5424) = 0.5814\n\n0.9938^33:\nln(0.9938) = -0.006219\n× 33 = -0.2052\nexp(-0.2052) = 0.8145\n\neGFR = 142 × 1 × 0.5814 × 0.8145 × 1.012\n= 142 × 0.5814 = 82.56\n× 0.8145 = 67.25\n× 1.012 = 68.06\n\nFINAL: 68"}